# Keeping the build context small makes the build faster and, more importantly, stops
# local state and secrets from being copied into an image layer.

**/bin
**/obj
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea

.git
.github

# Local runtime state. Copying a database or a Data Protection key ring into an image
# would bake one machine's data, and its decryptable tokens, into a distributable artifact.
data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

# Never build the credentials directory into an image. It is not used from A4 onward
# (configuration and environment variables replaced it), but a stale one may still exist
# in a working tree.
AUTH/

# Not needed to build or run the app.
tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
.env
.env.example

# Demo assets committed to the repo; several megabytes of no use to the image.
*.zip
project_thumbnail.png
